you may run into bugs or rough edges—please let us know if anything feels off.

DO I NEED DOCKER?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * NO DOCKER NEEDED:
    - Playing the game (Offline Bot Matches, Public/External Master Servers,
      and P2P Direct Play).
    - Joining a friend's hosted server.
    - Installing the `kongor` CLI and running the TAO MCP Server (`kongor mcp`).
    - Hosting Dedicated Match Servers (`COMPEL` / `COMPEL.GUI`) on Windows or
      Linux connecting to an existing Master Server.

  * DOCKER REQUIRED ONLY FOR SELF-HOSTED FULL STACK:
    - Only needed if you are hosting the complete backend cluster (Master Server,
      Chat Server, Web Portal, PostgreSQL 17, and Garnet cache) locally for your
      friends.


1. QUICK START — LAUNCHING THE GAME
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Keep WILLOWMAKER inside this `ProjectKongor` folder next to `games/`.

  * TIPS FOR WINDOWS TESTERS (FAST SETUP & FIREWALL):
    - Unblock the .zip before extracting:
      Right-click the downloaded .zip -> Properties -> check "Unblock" -> OK
      (or in PowerShell: Unblock-File <zip-path>). This prevents Windows SmartScreen
      ("Windows protected your PC") prompts on unsigned playtest executables.
      If you see SmartScreen: click "More info" -> "Run anyway".
    - Fast Extraction:
      Windows Explorer's built-in "Extract All" takes 30+ minutes on large
      archives. Using 7-Zip (Right-click -> 7-Zip -> Extract here) or PowerShell
      `tar -xf ProjectKongor-<build>-all.zip` finishes in ~90 seconds.
    - Windows Defender Firewall (Host Operators):
      When hosting for LAN/friends, Windows Firewall will prompt to allow access
      for KONGOR.MasterServer, TRANSMUTANSTEIN.ChatServer, DAWNBRINGER, or hon_x64.
      Allow access on BOTH "Private" and "Public" networks (in case your Wi-Fi is
      classified as a Public network profile), or friends will time out connecting.

  * Windows (`win-x64`):
    Double-click `WILLOWMAKER.exe`.

  * Linux (`linux-x64`):
    Run `./WILLOWMAKER` (or `./launcher-linux-x64/WILLOWMAKER` in multi-OS
    bundles) from Terminal. If your archive tool stripped execute permissions:
      chmod +x ./WILLOWMAKER ./launcher-linux-x64/WILLOWMAKER ./tools-linux-x64/kongor ./games/client/linux-x64/hon-x86_64 ./games/client/linux-x64/hon.sh

  * macOS (`osx-universal` — Apple Silicon & Intel):
    `HoN64` and its 64-bit `.dylib` modules are Universal-64 (`arm64` + `x86_64`).
    Because playtest builds are not Apple notarized, run the helper script once
    before first launch to clear Gatekeeper quarantine (`xattr -cr`) and apply
    local ad-hoc signatures (`codesign --force --sign -`):

      chmod +x ./macos-self-sign.command
      ./macos-self-sign.command

    Then run `./WILLOWMAKER` (or `./launcher-osx-arm64/WILLOWMAKER` on Apple
    Silicon / `./launcher-osx-x64/WILLOWMAKER` on Intel).


2. HOST FOR FRIENDS (SELF-HOSTED FULL STACK)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Host your own private Project Kongor cluster so friends can register accounts,
form parties, chat, and play dedicated matches on your server!

  * Prerequisite:
    Docker Desktop (Windows / macOS) or Docker Engine + Compose v2 (Linux)
    running locally. The cluster automatically provisions isolated
    `postgres:17-alpine` on `127.0.0.1:25432` and `garnet` on `127.0.0.1:28398`.

  * Launch Control Panel:
    - Windows : `control-panel-win-x64\NEXUS.ControlPanel.GUI.exe`
    - Linux   : `./control-panel-linux-x64/NEXUS.ControlPanel.GUI`
    - macOS (* experimental): `./control-panel-osx-arm64/NEXUS.ControlPanel.GUI`
      (Apple Silicon) or `./control-panel-osx-x64/NEXUS.ControlPanel.GUI` (Intel).
      (* Note: macOS hosts can run the control panel and backend services
      `master-server`, `chat-server`, `web-portal-api`, and `web-portal-ui`,
      while dedicated COMPEL K2 game servers require a Windows or Linux
      `compel-<rid>` host or P2P hosting.)

  * Hosting Modes (in the Dashboard "Hosting Mode" panel):
    - Local Only (`127.0.0.1`): For local practice and standalone testing.
    - LAN (`192.168.x.x` / `10.x.x.x`): For players on your local home network.
    - Tailscale / ZeroTier (`100.x.y.z`): Recommended zero-port-forwarding
      internet play with friends! Create a Tailscale mesh and host instantly.
    - Public Internet (WAN): For direct public hosting with port forwarding.

  * Security Note for Public Internet (WAN):
    The standalone web portal (`http://<host>:5266`) uses plain HTTP without
    TLS; tell friends to use a unique Kongor-only password and never reuse
    real-world passwords. (`ZORGATH` internal API remains strictly bound to
    `127.0.0.1:5200`.)

  * First-Boot Credentials & Friend Invite Codes:
    - Bootstrap admin credentials are written once to:
      `userdata/initial_admin_credentials.txt`
    - 10 single-use friend invite codes are generated at:
      `userdata/invite_codes.txt`
    - Generate more invite codes or create accounts anytime via CLI:
      `tools-<rid>/kongor invite create --count 10`
      `tools-<rid>/kongor account create --username <name> --password <pass>`

  * Firewall / Router Ports (for LAN & WAN hosts):
    - TCP: `55555` (Master Server), `5266` (Web Portal Sign-Up & Store/Codex),
           `11031-11033` (Chat Server)
    - UDP: `11235-11245` (Dedicated Game Servers) and `11735-11745` (Voice)
    - (Internal ports `5200`, `11234`, `25432`, `28398` are bound to `127.0.0.1`
      and must NEVER be port-forwarded.)

  * Linux Dedicated Server One-Time Host Prep:
    K2's native Linux server writes runtime configs under `/opt/hon/config`;
    run once before starting COMPEL on Linux:
      `sudo mkdir -p /opt/hon/config && sudo chown "$USER:$USER" /opt/hon/config`


3. JOIN A FRIEND'S SERVER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Joining a friend's hosted Project Kongor server takes less than a minute:

  1. Verify Build ID Parity:
     Ensure your bundle `Build ID` ({{BUILD_ID}}) matches your friend's host
     `Build ID`.
  2. Register Your Account:
     Open `http://<host-ip>:5266/Account/Register` in your web browser. Enter
     the single-use Invite Code provided by your host, choose your username,
     and enter a unique Kongor-only password.
     (New standalone accounts start with 10,000 Gold, 25,000 Silver, and 25
     Plinko Tickets!)
  3. Connect & Play:
     Launch `WILLOWMAKER` -> set Master Server to `<host-ip>:55555` -> click
     Play Online, sign in with your new account credentials, and join a hosted
     COMPEL match!


4. WAYS TO PLAY (NO DOCKER REQUIRED)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A) Offline Bot Matches:
     Open WILLOWMAKER, pick a map/mode (Forests of Caldavar, Mid Wars, Strikers,
     Capture The Flag, Team Deathmatch, Rift Wars, Devo Wars), and start a
     Practice / Bot Match.
     (macOS note: Master Server play and P2P Join are the most tested paths on
     macOS so far; offline bot mode on macOS is still experimental.)

  B) P2P Direct Play (Up to 10 Players):
     - Join (Windows / Linux / macOS): Enter the host's IP:Port (LAN, Tailscale,
       or ZeroTier works well) in WILLOWMAKER's P2P panel.
     - Host (Windows / Linux): Click Host P2P Match in WILLOWMAKER. The bundled
       `games/server_p2p/` server links client `.s2z` archives automatically.
       Forward UDP port `11235` if hosting over the internet.
     - macOS Host Note: There is no native macOS dedicated server binary; Mac
       users can join P2P games or host via a Linux Docker container.

  C) Local / Offline Auto & Community Master Servers (Project Kongor {{PLATFORM_VERSION}}):
     By default, WILLOWMAKER uses `Local / Offline Auto (localhost:55555)`:
     - If you are running a local `NEXUS` cluster on `:55555`, it connects online
       automatically.
     - Otherwise, clicking Play boots straight into the **Offline Main Menu Hub**
       (full 3D Avatar Store, Vault, Learnatorium, Seasonal Themes, Practice/Bot
       Matches, and P2P Hosting) with zero connection errors!
     - To join a friend's or community's hosted Master Server, select `Custom
       Address` (`<host-ip>:55555`) in WILLOWMAKER Settings. Leave "Pure 4.10
       Compatibility Mode" unchecked for Project Kongor `{{PLATFORM_VERSION}}` hosts; only enable
       it when connecting to an external legacy 4.10 server.

  D) Queue Arcade ("While You Wait" Skirmish Matches):
     When queued solo or in a party for Matchmaking, opt into Queue Arcade to jump
     instantly into a zero-stakes skirmish match against bots while waiting for
     your real match to pop. Skirmishes never affect your real rating or stats,
     and when your match is found, everyone is automatically pulled into the
     ranked game lobby with zero friction!


5. INSTALLING THE `kongor` CLI & TAO MCP SERVER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(Included in `tools-<rid>/`.)

To add `kongor` to your user `PATH` and sync `.mcp.json` to your OS (no admin
rights, `.NET SDK`, or Docker needed) so it works from any terminal directory:

  * Windows (PowerShell / CMD):
      .\tools-win-x64\kongor.exe install
      (or `.\tools-win-x64\kongor.exe refresh`)

  * Linux / macOS:
      ./tools-<rid>/kongor install
      (or `./tools-<rid>/kongor refresh`)

  * Zero-Config AI Agent Registration (TAO MCP Server):
    - Claude Code : `claude mcp add kongor -- ./tools-<rid>/kongor mcp`
                    (or open this folder after running `kongor install`—`.mcp.json`
                    and `CLAUDE.md` are pre-generated at the bundle root!)
    - Cursor      : Open this `ProjectKongor` folder after running `kongor install`;
                    `.mcp.json` is auto-discovered automatically.
    - Antigravity : `./tools-<rid>/kongor mcp --register-only`

Useful commands (run from any directory after `kongor install`):
  * `kongor`           — Status check for local services, ports, and VFS mounts
  * `kongor where`     — Show active Project Kongor bundle/workspace path
  * `kongor workspace` — List or switch registered Project Kongor installations
  * `kongor play`      — Launch WILLOWMAKER & game client
  * `kongor host`      — Launch COMPEL dedicated match server supervisor
  * `kongor gui`       — Open NEXUS Control Panel desktop GUI
  * `kongor start`     — Start local Master + Chat + Web Server stack
  * `kongor stop`      — Stop running Project Kongor background processes (scoped to active bundle)
  * `kongor mcp`       — Run the TAO MCP server over stdio for Claude Desktop,
                         Cursor, or Antigravity (UI/VFS inspection, replay parsing,
                         and local session tools)


6. DISPLAY (60 HZ TO 500 HZ) & WINDOWS PREREQUISITES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Display Defaults:
    First launch detects your monitor's refresh rate (60 Hz–500 Hz) and starts
    in Borderless Windowed mode to avoid fullscreen mode-switch issues. Engine
    FPS caps default to 1000; you can adjust VSync and frame limits in Settings.

  * Windows Prerequisites:
    - Windows uses DXVK v3.0.2 (Vulkan 1.3) to reduce shader compilation hitches.
    - Updated NVIDIA, AMD, or Intel GPU driver with Vulkan 1.3 support.
    - Microsoft Visual C++ x64 Redistributable:
      https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vc_redist.x64.exe


7. HOSTING DEDICATED SERVERS (`COMPEL` — NO DOCKER REQUIRED)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(Included under `compel-<rid>/`.)

  * Run `COMPEL.GUI` or `COMPEL` on Windows or Linux.
  * COMPEL links read-only `.s2z` archives from `games/client/` on first run.
  * Enter your Master Server URL and Host Account in `COMPEL.GUI` (or
    `compel-<rid>/COMPEL.json`). Remote HTTP control (`:11234`) stays disabled
    unless you configure your own `AuthenticationToken`.
  * UDP ports per match instance (`N = 0, 1, ...`): Game `11235 + N`,
    Voice `11735 + N`.


8. TESTER SHORTCUTS & LOCAL DIAGNOSTIC BUNDLES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * `Ctrl + Shift + D` in WILLOWMAKER : Open Developer Control Panel.
  * `Ctrl + Shift + D` In-Game        : Toggle Dev Cockpit (RmlUi on Windows,
                                        native K2 Dev Cockpit on Linux & macOS).

  * Reporting Crashes or Bugs:
    Crash dumps and logs are not uploaded automatically. If you hit a crash or
    issue, click "Export Diagnostics" in WILLOWMAKER to create a local `.zip`
    (`<= 8 MB`) that scrubs common tokens, passwords, IPs, and OS usernames.
    Please feel free to open and double-check the `.zip` contents before sending
    it in Discord just to be sure.

  * Note on Cold-Boot Watchdog Dumps:
    If you see a `hang_*_pid*.dmp` in your logs directory after first launching,
    this is a benign diagnostic snapshot captured by the launcher watchdog while
    the game engine was compiling Vulkan shaders during cold boot; no action is needed.


9. DEVELOPER & AI AGENT REFERENCE (`kongor mcp` LOCAL STACK SETUP)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(Optional reference for developers connecting Claude Desktop, Cursor, Copilot,
or Antigravity to `kongor mcp` to set up or test a local backend stack.)

  * Connecting Your Agent:
    Run `kongor refresh` first, then configure your MCP client to run
    `kongor mcp` over `stdio`.

  * Default Local Endpoints (Override via `host` / `masterServer` if needed):
    - PostgreSQL 17 (`MERRICK`) : `127.0.0.1:25432` (Docker) or `127.0.0.1:5432`
    - Garnet / Redis Cache      : `127.0.0.1:28398` (Docker) or `127.0.0.1:28298`
    - Master Server             : `127.0.0.1:55555`
    - Chat Server               : `127.0.0.1:11031` (HTTPS `:5554`)
    - Web Portal UI / API       : `127.0.0.1:5266` / `127.0.0.1:5200`
    - COMPEL Control Plane      : `127.0.0.1:11234` (Local), `:11334` (Docker),
                                  `:11434` (K3s / Agones)

  * Keep Player & Dedicated-Host (`svr_login`) Accounts Separate:
    COMPEL authenticates to the Master Server using a Host Account (`svr_login`).
    Use separate accounts for playing vs. hosting—and if you run multiple COMPEL
    fleets at the same time (e.g., Local + Docker + K3s), give each fleet its
    own Host Account so their `svr_login` sessions do not kick each other off.
    Accounts and tokens can be managed in `NEXUS.ControlPanel.GUI` ("Users" and
    "Secrets & Config" tabs), the Web Portal, or via `kongor_db_fixture`.

  * Recommended 4-Step Bootstrap Sequence for Agents:
    1. Start Stack     : `kongor_server_manage` (`action: "start"`,
                         `target: "cluster"`) or "Start Cluster" in Control Panel.
    2. Schema & Users  : `KONGOR.MasterServer` runs schema initialization and
                         catalog seeding on startup; use `kongor_db_fixture` /
                         `kongor_db_pool_diagnostics` (and `kongor_db_migrate`
                         when running with EF migrations) to verify DB readiness
                         and ensure both Player and distinct Host accounts exist.
    3. Verify Health   : `kongor_health_check` and `kongor_diagnostics` (tool
                         responses include remediation hints if a port or config
                         check fails).
    4. Launch & Test   : `kongor_compel_manage` (`action: "start"` / `"instances"`)
                         and `kongor_game_client_manage` / `kongor_client_eval_lua`
                         to start dedicated workers and verify a local match.


